.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt CTLOG_STORE_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm CTLOG_STORE_new_ex ,
.Nm CTLOG_STORE_new ,
.Nm CTLOG_STORE_free ,
.Nm CTLOG_STORE_load_default_file ,
.Nm CTLOG_STORE_load_file
.Nd Create and populate a Certificate Transparency log list
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ct.h
.Ft CTLOG_STORE *
.Fo CTLOG_STORE_new_ex
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft CTLOG_STORE *
.Fo CTLOG_STORE_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo CTLOG_STORE_free
.Fa "CTLOG_STORE *store"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo CTLOG_STORE_load_default_file
.Fa "CTLOG_STORE *store"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo CTLOG_STORE_load_file
.Fa "CTLOG_STORE *store"
.Fa "const char *file"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A CTLOG_STORE is a container for a list of CTLOGs (Certificate
Transparency logs).
The list can be loaded from one or more files and then searched by LogID
(see RFC 6962, Section 3.2, for the definition of a LogID).
.Pp
.Fn CTLOG_STORE_new_ex
creates an empty list of CT logs associated with the library context
.Fa libctx
and the property query string
.Fa propq .
.Pp
.Fn CTLOG_STORE_new
does the same thing as
.Fn CTLOG_STORE_new_ex
but with the default library context and property query string.
.Pp
The CTLOG_STORE is then populated by
.Fn CTLOG_STORE_load_default_file
or
.Fn CTLOG_STORE_load_file .
.Fn CTLOG_STORE_load_default_file
loads from the default file, which is named
.Pa ct_log_list.cnf
in OPENSSLDIR (see the output of
.Xr openssl-version 1 Ns ).
This can be overridden using an environment variable named
.Sy CTLOG_FILE .
.Fn CTLOG_STORE_load_file
loads from a caller-specified file path instead.
Both of these functions append any loaded CT logs to the CTLOG_STORE.
.Pp
The expected format of the file is:
.Bd -literal
 enabled_logs=foo,bar

 [foo]
 description = Log 1
 key = <base64-encoded DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo here>

 [bar]
 description = Log 2
 key = <base64-encoded DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo here>
.Ed
.Pp
Once a CTLOG_STORE is no longer required, it should be passed to
.Fn CTLOG_STORE_free .
This will delete all of the CTLOGs stored within, along with the
CTLOG_STORE itself.
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Sh NOTES
If there are any invalid CT logs in a file, they are skipped and the
remaining valid logs will still be added to the CTLOG_STORE. A CT log
will be considered invalid if it is missing a "key" or "description"
field.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Both
.Sy CTLOG_STORE_load_default_file
and
.Sy CTLOG_STORE_load_file
return 1 if all CT logs in the file are successfully parsed and loaded,
0 otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ct 7 ,
.Xr CTLOG_STORE_get0_log_by_id 3 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_ctlog_list_file 3
.Sh HISTORY
CTLOG_STORE_new_ex was added in OpenSSL 3.0. All other functions were
added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
